# Shared File Dropzone — Task Plan & Implementation Log

## Plan
- High-level goal: Extract a reusable `FileDropzone.vue` component to provide a consistent, modern drag-and-drop file upload experience across Common Documents and Program Accreditation.
- Scope:
  - Create `resources/js/Components/FileDropzone.vue` with drag-and-drop, file type validation, size formatting, and file preview/remove pill.
  - Refactor `UploadCommonDocModal.vue` to use `FileDropzone`.
  - Refactor `UploadDocumentModal.vue` (Program Accreditation) to use `FileDropzone`.
  - Ensure both modal components stay well under the 150-line modularity rule.
- Key decisions:
  - Component supports `v-model` binding with a native `File` object or `null`.
  - Flexible props: `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `hint`, `error`, and institutional `color` ('blue' | 'orange').
  - Automatically formats file size using `tabular-nums` and standard byte units.
  - Standard DaisyUI components (`fieldset`, `legend`, `btn`, `btn-circle`, `btn-ghost`, `border-dashed`).
- Testing strategy:
  - Frontend build verification with `npm run build`.
  - Feature test verification with `php artisan test`.

